\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces A/B forecasting check for normalized linear decoder atoms on the retained Dysts \(dt{\times }30\) benchmark. The left block repeats the current paper table, while the two normalized-decoder blocks compare rollout-latent and encoded-latent sparsity targets. These rows are shown as a replacement candidate audit rather than a table replacement because the normalized-decoder packets still have missing retained-system seed runs: \(7\) for rollout-latent sparsity and \(3\) for encoded-latent sparsity.}}{9}{table.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ab_normdec_dysts_forecasting}{{3}{9}{A/B forecasting check for normalized linear decoder atoms on the retained Dysts \(dt{\times }30\) benchmark. The left block repeats the current paper table, while the two normalized-decoder blocks compare rollout-latent and encoded-latent sparsity targets. These rows are shown as a replacement candidate audit rather than a table replacement because the normalized-decoder packets still have missing retained-system seed runs: \(7\) for rollout-latent sparsity and \(3\) for encoded-latent sparsity}{table.caption.15}{}}
